      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>Pointeworks primary exempt purpose is to advance the performing arts by providing opportunities for professional dancers choreographers and musicians to collaborate and create. The organization focuses on amplifying diverse voices in dance particularly empowering female choreographers while delivering high-quality performances and community outreach initiatives that make the arts accessible to underserved audiences.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Program Title 1: 2024 Ballet Season Pointeworks 2024 ballet season ran from April to June and culminated in a sold-out performance at the Conrad Prebys Performing Arts Center on June 20. The program employed 12 dancers 5 female choreographers 1 musician 1 composer 1 designer and 1 stage manager fostering artistic collaboration and amplifying female voices in the performing arts. The season benefited 450 attendees including underserved community members such as veterans and students through ticket donations. Pointeworks also collaborated with mental health and wellness departments to extend the therapeutic benefits of the arts and engaged with the local Rotary Club to strengthen community ties.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
